WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.933
Build an estimate: sections, materials, add-ons.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:10.300
Open an estimate. Sections are built on the estimate. The tour opens this one.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:22.067
The section bar. Each section is one line on the estimate. Its bar holds the name, the tax switch, the section total and the tools to fold, move or remove it.

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:31.867
Fold it away. The arrow folds a section to one line so a long estimate is easy to read. The tax switch and the total stay visible.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:41.433
Section name. What the customer reads as the line title, e.g. Paver patio. Every section needs a name before you can save.

00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:53.567
Taxable or Tax exempt. One click switches it; the sales tax follows. The Taxable tick inside the section does the same. Catalogue services bring their own setting.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:01:01.700
Section total. Quantity × labor price, plus every material line at its price. It updates as you type.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:09.300
Move up or down. The arrows change the order the customer reads the sections in. Nothing is deleted.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:17.400
Remove a section. Takes the section and its materials off (it asks first). Nothing is final until you press Save.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:25.533
What the customer reads. Describe the work in plain words. This text is printed under the section name on the estimate.

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:36.400
Quantity and unit. How many, and of what (sq ft, job, ea, ft). After you measure, "Use a measurement" buttons appear here and fill both in one click.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:43.433
Labor price per unit. Your price for the work, per unit. The materials below are added on top.

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:51.400
Crew-hours (budget). How long the crew needs. It sizes the job on the Schedule and feeds the Margin card.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:02:01.000
Optional add-on. Tick it for an extra the customer can choose, like lighting. It's priced apart and kept out of the total until they take it.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:10.333
Note for the crew. Gas line, access, where to dump spoils… It goes on the job and the work order, never on the customer's copy.

00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:21.000
Materials. Material, quantity, unit, your cost, the customer's price and the line amount. Cost stays inside the office; it drives the margin.

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:32.600
Hidden or shown lines. Unticked (the default), a line is hidden: the customer sees only the section total. Tick Show to list it on their copy, without its price.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:39.267
Reorder or remove lines. The arrows move a line up or down; the x removes it.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:47.933
Add a material. Search the catalogue by name or category and pick one: it comes in with its unit, cost and price.

00:02:48.433 --> 00:02:55.467
Blank line. For a material that isn't in the catalogue: type the name, quantity, cost and price yourself.

00:02:55.967 --> 00:03:03.967
An optional add-on. Dashed and marked Optional. The customer ticks it on the online link, or you tick it when you press Won.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:15.233
Add a section from the catalogue. Pick a service: it brings its price, unit, crew-hours and tax setting, plus its kit of materials (hidden unless the kit says show).

00:03:15.733 --> 00:03:19.600
Blank section. An empty section to fill in yourself.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:27.800
Totals. Subtotal, sales tax on the taxable sections and the total, plus "Optional add-ons (not in total)".

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:35.733
Margin. Cost, gross profit, margin % and crew-hours, as you build. Never shown to the customer.

00:03:36.233 --> 00:03:45.167
Save it. Nothing is kept until you press Save (or ⌘S / Ctrl+S); "Unsaved changes" reminds you. The tour doesn't save.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:51.267
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
